# A LABEL CARRIES THE INLINE VOCABULARY, READ-ONLY (docs/rich-text-plan.md
# R8, §15): the app writes and edits its document, and every arm draws the
# runs over the role's own font. The widget's runs are read beside the
# core's on every lane (the corroboration wall).
expect label#0 ""
expect_runs label#0 ""
click button#0
expect label#0 "Héllo world, code"
expect_runs label#0 "0:6 bold|7:12 link=https://kaya.dev|14:18 code"
expect label#2 "0:6 bold|7:12 link=https://kaya.dev|14:18 code"
expect label#1 "Heading with italic"
expect_runs label#1 "13:19 italic"
click button#1
expect label#0 "Héllo, big world, code"
expect_runs label#0 "0:6 bold|8:11 italic|12:17 link=https://kaya.dev|19:23 code"
expect label#2 "0:6 bold|8:11 italic|12:17 link=https://kaya.dev|19:23 code"
